# AgenticPacks OSS Cursor Rules & Architectural Directives

## 1. Strict Layer Architecture
- **React Components (`src/components/`, `src/app/`)**: MUST NEVER call Prisma directly (`prisma.user.find...`, `$queryRaw`, etc.). All data mutations and database queries must go through the dedicated service functions in `src/services/` or server actions/API route handlers.
- **Service Layer (`src/services/`)**: All business logic, AI completion, token accounting, and Prisma operations live here.
- **Library Layer (`src/lib/`)**: Shared utilities, database client singleton (`db.ts`), environment schema (`env.ts`), logger (`logger.ts`), and error hierarchy (`errors.ts`).

## 2. Service Function Return Signatures
All service functions must return a strict Discriminated Union:
```typescript
type Result<T> = 
  | { success: true; data: T } 
  | { success: false; error: AppError; code: string };
```
Never throw unhandled errors in service functions; catch, log with `logger`, and return `{ success: false, error, code }`.

## 3. Type Safety
- TypeScript strict mode is enabled. NEVER use `any`. Use `unknown`, generic constraints, or explicit Zod inference types (`z.infer<typeof Schema>`).
- Validate all incoming request bodies using Zod schemas located in `src/lib/validation/`. Use the `withValidation` wrapper on API endpoints.

## 4. Design & Mobile Responsiveness
- All UI components must be mobile-first and fully responsive across 375px (iPhone SE) to 1440px+ desktop viewports.
- Use shadcn/ui components and Tailwind CSS design tokens. No inline raw hex styles.

## 5. OSS Invariants
- **Credits in Postgres only**: Never put wallet balance on the JWT/session. Session may carry `id` / `role` / `plan`; UI syncs credits via DB, `/api/user/profile`, and `credits-updated`.
- **Fail closed**: Chat and billing APIs require auth. No synthetic `demo-user`. Do not call OpenAI if the DB is down or the wallet is empty (402 / 503).
- **Stripe idempotency**: Webhooks must persist `StripeEvent` (event id) in the same transaction as plan/credit updates; duplicates return HTTP 200.
- **Password change**: If `passwordHash` exists, require and verify `currentPassword` before updating.
- **Scope**: Free + Pro ($19) only. No Redis, rate limiting, teams, RAG, or LangGraph. Never use $149 as an in-app SaaS plan price.
- Prefer `services/` + `Result<T>`; no Prisma in React (see §1).
